      "writtenOn": "2019-07-05T13:44:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This seems quite brittle because it could break if the Vpn class changes. If it really depends on the implementation details of that class, then it should be a method of that class. (If we don\u0027t have that class here... then why don\u0027t we? Perhaps for VPNs we could add a pointer from the NetworkAgentInfo object to the Vpn object for that network? Is the problem that we can\u0027t do that because we\u0027re running on the wrong thread?)\n\nThat said, I\u0027m not convinced that this depends on the implementation details of Vpn. A VPN is \"in force\" if its UID rules are applied, right? If so, then... the class that applies those rules is ConnectivityService. So perhaps the logic here should use ConnectivityService internal data structures instead of looking at the state of the Vpn object.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1956,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 1960,
        "endChar": 64
      },
      "revId": "d5a66ae641e13403a78c5225b45ac4a43b6ae4eb",
